    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Kyndryl is a public company, traded as KD, that was founded in 2021 and is headquartered in New York, NY, USA. Its SEC filing identifier is 0001867072. On its own site, the company describes itself as designing, building, managing and modernizing the mission-critical technology systems that the world depends on every day.\n\nThe site's AI material centers on workforce readiness and enterprise adoption. Kyndryl's 2026 People Readiness Report, described as revealing a decline in workforce readiness as AI adoption surges, explores why readiness has become one of the most important factors determining AI success. The company also describes AI-native enterprises as those that create conditions for continuous growth, efficiency and resilience by putting AI at the core of their business, and it hosts a podcast, The Innovation Show x The Kyndryl Institute, in which five leaders discuss how AI is evolving current business models. A further item on the site notes that as geopolitical tensions escalate and AI accelerates attackers' capabilities, organizations must rethink what resilience looks like in the context of prosperity, security and public trust. No specific AI products are tracked for the company, and no MCP servers are listed.\n\nThe litigation record held for Kyndryl is concentrated in New York, with 458 cases counted there. No individual cases are listed.",
